    "updated_at": "2020-05-20T10:28:36Z",
    "body": "The one-line shell installer is insane. Don't ever pipe anything unknown from the web into your (root) shell.\r\nAnd besides that, it knows nothing about the current installation, so if you have installed into another bindir (because the default one `/usr/local/bin` isn't writeable without root), you have to give this option for every new invocation.",
