    "created_at": "2020-05-20T12:39:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-20T12:39:32Z",
    "body": "I agree that really it shouldn't run as root and instead could just install to a location in the user's home directory like Rust does with it's rustup installer.\r\n\r\nYou could install to `$HOME/.local/bin` as I don't think it would be appropriate to create a whole new non-standard directory like rustup does ie. when it creates `$HOME/.cargo`",
