    "created_at": "2020-05-20T18:55:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-20T18:55:36Z",
    "body": "We could mimic the behaviour of the rustup installer in the way that it adds the directory to the PATH\r\n\r\nWith a snippet like this which will only add `$HOME/.local/bin` to the `PATH` if it isn't already in it\r\n```bash\r\nif ! echo \"$PATH\" | tr ':' '\\n' | grep \"$HOME/.local/bin\"; then\r\n    # shellcheck disable=SC2016\r\n    echo 'export PATH=$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH' >> \"$HOME\"/.profile\r\nfi\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote: We have to disable the shellcheck warning otherwise it complains about the single quotes which in this case is a false positive because we don't want the variable expansion",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
